    "long_instructions": "## Accessing Properties \r\n\r\n#### Now that you have learned how to identify data in JSON, we are going to focus on how to access the correct piece of data. \r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;\">📖 <strong>Dot Notation </strong>  is a way to access properties inside JavaScript objects by chaining property names with dots from left to right.\r\n</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n#### Take a look at the diagram below to understand how properties and objects are connected with dot notation. \r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/ebdc99a8f0e40584ec19cbef74fe38a3-image-1772122722177.png\" alt=\"diagram illustrating the property name of object user being connected with dot notation to access the data john.\" width=\"450px\" style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;border-radius:10px; \">\r\n\r\n---\r\n## Tracing Dot Notation\r\n\r\n#### The video below explains the process in JavaScript. Watch the video for an explanation and then try on you own in the next level. \r\n"
  },
